        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c879ed7b-532e-5b24-842c-ef83dfdba6a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sidney Olcott, Denis Villeneuve\n- Roles: film producer, director, actor, screenwriter, writer\n- Awards: Canadian Screen Award, Genie Award, Best Direction\n- Works: Maelström, Polytechnique, Incendies, Enemy\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Olcott was born on September 20, 1872, and was a Canadian-born film producer, director, actor, and screenwriter.\n- Denis Villeneuve was born on October 3, 1967, and is a French Canadian film director and writer.\n- In 2001, Denis Villeneuve received the Canadian Screen Award, formerly called the Genie Award, for Best Direction for Maelström.\n- In 2010, Denis Villeneuve received the Canadian Screen Award for Best Direction for Polytechnique.\n- In 2011, Denis Villeneuve received the Canadian Screen Award for Best Direction for Incendies.\n- In 2013, Denis Villeneuve received the Canadian Screen Award for Best Direction for Enemy.\n- Denis Villeneuve is a four-time recipient of the Canadian Screen Award for Best Direction.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "595f5c79-12d2-5d0f-805b-e15bfed01115",
        "text": "Page: Sidney Olcott. Sentence: Sidney Olcott (September 20, 1872 – December 16, 1949) was a Canadian-born film producer, director, actor and screenwriter.\nPage: Denis Villeneuve. Sentence: Denis Villeneuve (] ; born October 3, 1967) is a French Canadian film director and writer.\nPage: Denis Villeneuve. Sentence: He is a four-time recipient of the Canadian Screen Award (formerly Genie Award) for Best Direction, for \"Maelström\" in 2001, \"Polytechnique\" in 2010, \"Incendies\" in 2011, and \"Enemy\" in 2013.",
